<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reynosa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1749">1749</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reynosa is a city in the Mexican state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamaulipas">Tamaulipas</a>, on the south bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a> opposite McAllen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>. It was founded in 1749 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-escandon">José de Escandón</a> as one of the first settlements of the colony of Nuevo Santander. Since the late 20th century it has grown into a large industrial city of export factories, or maquiladoras.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reynosa.jpg" alt="Reynosa" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robox91 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_desde_el_tejado.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
